x86_64-windows  the closure names, the difference lambda.nonames records: clang calls a closure `<lambda_N>` in the local scope `?0?` where cxx1 writes `$_N` in `?1?`, and the call operator, the conversion function `??B` and the static `__invoke` carry that name. Nothing links against them - a closure is a unique unnamed type, [expr.prim.lambda]. On the two Itanium targets every name agrees, the conversion `_ZZ4mainENK3$_0cvPFiiEEv` and `_ZZ4mainEN3$_08__invokeEi` among them.
